<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaluit Gesellschaft</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1887–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Jaluit Company</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jaluit Gesellschaft was a German trading company formed in 1887 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> firms engaged in the copra trade of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a>. From 1888 it paid the costs of administering the German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in return for a monopoly of trade and land rights, so the colony was in effect run by a company. Its administrative role ended in 1906.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaluit-gesellschaft.jpg" alt="Jaluit Gesellschaft" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fornax · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaluit_Gesellschaft_Var2.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
